Whitespace-bearing values round-trip rather than being mangled or rejected: a tab lands as a
double-quoted escape and a newline as a folded single-quoted block, each reloading as the
text that was given. The newline arrives through a Jinja string literal — a command line
cannot carry a raw one.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
---
# Body
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md 'tabbed=a	b' 'lined={{ "x\ny" }}'
-- exit --
0
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: tabbed=a	b, lined=x
y
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
tabbed: "a\tb"
lined: 'x

  y'
---
# Body
